# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESTRICTED DATA — DO NOT REMOVE
#
# data/ holds licensed content that must never be committed:
#   - MIMIC-IV note text, under the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data Use
#     Agreement. Ship data/notes.sql (the extraction query) instead.
#   - The UMLS Metathesaurus, under the UMLS Metathesaurus License Agreement,
#     and everything derived from it (QuickUMLS indexes, lexicons, edge lists).
#   - Corpora with no attached licence (NegEx, BioScope, CASI), which this
#     project treats exactly like MIMIC. MTSamples is CC0 but is still kept
#     out of the repository: it is 17 MB of text nothing in src/ needs.
#
# The data/ block is DEFAULT-DENY on purpose. An allowlist of extensions is one
# unanticipated file type away from leaking (a .zip, a .RRF, a differently
# cased directory), so everything under data/ is ignored and the few
# publishable files are re-admitted by name.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Git applies the LAST matching rule, so the belt-and-braces
# directory patterns (**/umls/, **/quickumls_index/) sit ABOVE the data/
# block: the block re-admits data/umls/ and data/quickumls_index/ so that
# their placeholder READMEs can be tracked, and the same global pattern placed
# below the block would silently re-exclude them. Add new global directory
# patterns to the belt-and-braces group, never after the data/ block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Belt-and-braces: these must never be committed from anywhere in the tree,
# whatever they are called or wherever they are dropped.
*.RRF
*.rrf
*.zip
*.duckdb
**/[Uu][Mm][Ll][Ss]/
**/[Mm][Ee][Tt][Aa]/
# QuickUMLS indexes — derived from licensed UMLS content, never committed
**/quickumls_index/
**/quickumls_snomed/
*.unqlite

# data/: deny everything, then re-admit the publishable files by name.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/notes.sql

# Placeholder directories, each holding only a README.md that says what goes
# there and how to obtain or build it. Git cannot re-admit a file whose parent
# directory is ignored, so each directory is re-admitted by name; `data/*/*`
# then denies everything inside every re-admitted directory, and
# `!data/*/README.md` lets only the README back through. Adding a directory is
# ONE line here plus its README -- the deny-contents rule is shared, so it
# cannot be forgotten. A directory listed here must contain a README.md.
!data/umls/
!data/quickumls_index/
!data/snomed_el/
!data/negex/
!data/bioscope/
!data/drugs/
!data/lexicon/
!data/casi/
!data/assertion_gold_mimic/
!data/phenotype_review/
!data/mtsamples/
data/*/*
!data/*/README.md

# Manuscript drafts. Written beside the code, never versioned with it: nothing
# in src/, tests/ or validation/ reads them. Unanchored on purpose, so a copy
# dropped anywhere in the tree is ignored as well.
manuscript/
old_manuscript/

# Derived artifacts that may embed restricted text
**/annotations.parquet
**/*.annotations.json
.robustehr_cache/
out/
runs/
release/text/

# Secrets
#
# API keys are read from the environment first and from these files as a
# fallback. They are matched by name rather than by extension because a `.txt`
# allowlist elsewhere would otherwise re-admit them — the same default-deny
# reasoning the data/ block uses.
.env
secrets/
openrouterapi.txt
*api*key*.txt
*_api.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv*/
.tox/
.nox/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.hypothesis/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Downloaded experiment results: derived from MIMIC-IV under the PhysioNet DUA,
# and 200 MB+ per run. The bucket is the system of record; a local copy is a
# working convenience, not something to version.
results/

# Experiment run directories. `run1/` held a 163 MB SQLite prediction store whose
# `document_id` column is real MIMIC `hadm_id`s — derived restricted data under the
# PhysioNet DUA, and it sat here untracked but unignored. `runs/` above covers the
# corruption engine's own output; this covers the downstream harness's, which names
# its directories by run id.
run[0-9]*/

# Prediction stores and any other embedded database. Matched by extension as well as
# by directory because a run directory can be renamed and the SQLite file inside it is
# still a SQLite file — the same default-deny reasoning the data/ block uses.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
